  "Radar only, one ascending track (158, frame 27): the motion is drawn as if it were all vertical. The study's bowls use an ascending and a descending track; the two can differ where the ground also moves sideways.",
  "NISAR GUNW PROVISIONAL, about 4 months (25 Jun – 11 Oct 2026): rates are early, not validated against EGMS or levelling yet.",
  "Zero point (ref_bbox) chosen after looking at the study's vertical map: a coherent town south of the mined field (post-hoc).",
  "Post-hoc: the first build showed a broad -10 to -16 cm/yr patch in the south-east where all three study tracks give ~0, so a long-wavelength filter was added (sigma 5 km, fast features masked at 8 cm/yr + 0.5 km, the study's values; detection on a 400 m smoothed rate, chosen here).",
  "Post-hoc: strokes are drawn down to coherence 0.3 (the study's threshold), lowered from 0.45 because the bowls have coherence 0.41-0.45.",
